# ── What the review established ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ A DataVolume's SPEC IS IMMUTABLE AFTER CREATION. CDI's validating webhook refuses an update that
# changes `spec`, and a PersistentVolumeClaim's request can never decrease; expansion is a change to
# the claim and depends on the class's allowVolumeExpansion. That is why every tenant-facing value in
# this chart is @immutable, and why `resize-is-not-offered` is an owed row rather than a property.
#
# ⚠ `spec.storage` VERSUS `spec.pvc`, AND WHAT THE FIRST REAL RUN CORRECTED. The `storage` form lets
# CDI fill accessModes and volumeMode from the StorageProfile it keeps per class. This file said CDI
# "falls back to ReadWriteOnce/Filesystem for a class it has no profile entry for", and it does not:
# on 2026-09-17 the first DataVolume applied to a real CDI 1.66 sat on `no accessMode specified in
# StorageProfile openebs-hostpath` and never bound. CDI's table of known provisioners has no
# openebs.io/local row, and with no entry it fills nothing. So accessModes is written — ReadWriteOnce —
# and only the volume mode is left to the profile; conformance.yaml § owed,
# `access-mode-is-read-write-once`, carries what that costs and the bundle's half.
#
# ⚠ THE PHASES A BLANK DISK PASSES THROUGH ON A WaitForFirstConsumer CLASS: Pending → WaitForFirstConsumer
# (or PendingPopulation under CDI's populator path) → Bound and Succeeded once a pod mounts it. The
# reconciler calls the middle one converged — Cdi.IsProvisioned — because nothing consumes a disk
# until a machine does, and KubeVirt's own VM controller treats the same two phases as ready
# (pkg/virt-controller/watch/vm/vm.go, handleDataVolumes).
upstream-webhook: CDI ships a validating webhook for DataVolume (spec immutability, source shape, a clone's source claim must exist) and a mutating one that fills spec.storage from the StorageProfile
